        ":question/problem": "Calculate $C-D$, where\n$C=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 12 & -1 \\\\ 6 & -7 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $D=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -8 & -1 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n| $C-D=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} |  |  |",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We subtract the corresponding entries:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C-D & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 12 & -1 \\\\ 6 & -7 & 3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -8 & -1 & 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4-(-9) & 12-5 & -1-2 \\\\ 6-(-8) & -7-(-1) & 3-10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 14 & -6 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
