        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-319622",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate $G-H$, where\n$G=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 7 \\\\ -6 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -8\\end{bmatrix}$ and $H=\\begin{bmatrix}10 & -5 \\\\ -6 & -9 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n| $G-H=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |\n|  | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} |  |  |",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We subtract the corresponding entries:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G-H & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 7 \\\\ -6 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -8\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}10 & -5 \\\\ -6 & -9 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7-10 & 7-(-5) \\\\ -6-(-6) & 2-(-9) \\\\ 5-3 & -8-(-1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 11 \\\\ 2 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
