        ":question/id": "43b3f28f-92d2-5c8b-adfb-c1420a9c589a",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-319625",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate $P-Q$, where\n$P=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 10 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $Q=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -7 \\\\ 12 & -5 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n| $P-Q=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | $3$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $11$ | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |\n|  | {{field-5}} | $5$ | {{field-6}} |  |  |",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We subtract the corresponding entries:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P-Q & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 10 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -7 \\\\ 12 & -5 & 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6-1 & 4-(-8) & 9-6 \\\\ 7-(-4) & -2-3 & 5-(-7) \\\\ 10-12 & 0-(-5) & -3-9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & \\,\\,12 & 3 \\\\ \\,\\,\\,11 & -5 & 12 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -12\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
